WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.268 line:92%
-New York, New York, New York.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.336 line:92%
All right, calm down. Calm down.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to catch the 2 train
in a minute.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm 26.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.442 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Yeah, I'm an adult now.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't like it.
I don't like it.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:11.845 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was tricked.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mom told me,
"When you get grown,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can do
whatever you want to do."

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not true.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.219
When you're grown, you can do
whatever you can afford to do.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's different.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Paying bills.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
I miss free fun.
I miss free fun.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
I miss playing tag
because I was never it.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.499
All my friends knew if I was it,
that was it.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.666 line:92%
That's the end of the game.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.168 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not chasing you
around no neighborhood.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.671 size:84% position:42%
The living room, maybe.
Not the neighborhood.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not chasing you
around the neighborhood.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I hated freeze tag.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's got to be
the dumbest game ever.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
They only play it
on the hottest day.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tag, you can't move.
Like, wait, wait.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.548
You couldn't have froze me
in the shade over there?

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.818
I'm-a thaw out over here.
I don't know if you know.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.186 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:56.222
I hung out with everybody.
I don't care about your race.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.491 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I don't care, you know.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.559 line:92%
White, black, I don't care.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
My favorite friend was white,
named Tanner.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tanner had
the best post-play snacks.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.501 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
One time we was playing
at his house,

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.804 line:92%
he pulled out some Lunchables.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it messed me up
because I didn't even know

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
you could eat Lunchables
at home.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:19.145 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:23.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought you had to be
in school to eat Lunchables.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.184 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was so excited.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
I ate two semesters worth of
Lunchables at his house.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:28.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:32.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. It was a new experience.
That's what life's about.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.293 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
New experiences.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.161 size:81% position:41%
That's where, I think,
racism comes from --

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
lack of experiences or doing
stuff with other people.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do your favorite thing
with other races.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was blessed to do that
as a kid growing up.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.803
Like, my favorite thing to do
growing up was sleepovers.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.305 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Remember sleepovers?

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, go over somebody else's
house,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
mess their stuff up,
then go home.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:49.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember the first time
I slept over Tanner's house.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was amazing.
I learned so much about --

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:54.714 line:92%
I didn't know you can make

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
so much noise
at white people's house

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.817 line:92%
and their parents don't get mad.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.487 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.187 line:92%
It's 3:00 in the morning.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.556
All you hear is Tanner's dad go,
"Tanner, what in tarnations?"

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.959 size:78% position:39%
I was like, "Hold on.
What's tarnations?"

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.260 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tanner was like,
"I'm sorry, Father.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're just playing
a game of tag."

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
His dad got mad.
He was like, "Without me?"

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:13.833 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.036
He said, "Okay, I got something
for you busters 'cause I'm it.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
One, two."

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.442 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I just froze.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I never heard
no black parent count up.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:33.486 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Unh-unh.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they will count down
on you fast.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:36.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.958
And my mama was so gangster,
she would count and name a chore

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
that better magically be done
in between each number.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.830
She'd just start out threatening
everybody like,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Y'all got five seconds
to be in that bed.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm talking about
in the bed,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
not on your way to the bed,
not by the bed.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm talking about I want
knees in sheets.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Five.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
And your clothes better be
ironed for school

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the morning too.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Four.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
And your teeth better be
brushed.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Three.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there better be some gas
in my car

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause if there ain't no gas
in my car --"

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.419 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.522
Like, I'm in kindergarten. That
ain't got nothing to do with me.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:16.229 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Learn, people, man.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to learn about
being with them.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like I know,
as a young black kid,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.969
I grew up thinking
white kids didn't get whoopings.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's not true.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not white kids
don't get physical whoopings,

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it be mental.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
White parents
say stuff to their kids

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they need counseling
before they hit 33.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.548 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you wouldn't know that
if you're not there.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:38.751 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I'm at Tanner's house.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
what he did at school,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
but his daddy would snap.
He was like, "You know what?

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is some real malarkey,
pal."

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:44.991 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I said, "Oh."

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:45.792 line:92%
He said, "Jesus H. Christ."

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.461
I say, "Hold on, Jesus got
a middle name? I didn't --"

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.531 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:52.632 line:92%
That's when I knew it was over.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like,
"You know what, Tanner?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.668 line:92%
I'm so -- I'm so mad at you.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.603 line:92%
Your grandfather's probably

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
turning over in his grave
right now."

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:02.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Damn."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:02.942 size:88% position:44% line:92%
What can you actually do

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
for somebody to turn over
in their grave?

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.780 line:92%
Like, can you imagine that?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, he just failed Spanish
again.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:13.019 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:17.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
Como se dice?
Como se dice?

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:20.126
It made me think, because my
grandaddy got a messed-up hip.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.096
So somebody got to go down there
and help him turn over.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:24.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm Leonard Ouzts.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank y'all so much.
I appreciate you.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:31.971 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.775 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:39.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
Leonard Ouzts!
Leonard Ouzts!

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:43.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
See him Thursday nights
starring in "Abby's" on NBC.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Very funny show.

